# order-service REST API (REQUIREMENTS.md §7). Run from IntelliJ or VS Code (REST Client).
# Prices are decimal amounts in EUR. Errors are RFC 9457 Problem Details (application/problem+json).

@host = http://localhost:8080
@customerId = 0192f0c1-0000-7000-8000-000000000003
@restaurantId = 0192f0c1-0000-7000-8000-000000000004
@productId = 0192f0c1-0000-7000-8000-000000000005

### Create an order -> 202 with the tracking id
# @name createOrder
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "restaurantId": "{{restaurantId}}",
  "address": { "street": "Main Street 1", "postalCode": "10115", "city": "Berlin" },
  "price": 50.00,
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{productId}}", "quantity": 2, "price": 25.00, "subTotal": 50.00 }
  ],
  "notes": "No onions please, I'm allergic to peanuts. Ring twice."
}

### Track the order created above -> 200
GET {{host}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.orderTrackingId}}

### Unknown tracking id -> 404
GET {{host}}/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Invalid order (no items, blank street) -> 400 with the violations
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "restaurantId": "{{restaurantId}}",
  "address": { "street": " ", "postalCode": "10115", "city": "Berlin" },
  "price": 50.00,
  "items": []
}

### Preview how order notes are interpreted, without placing an order -> 200
POST {{host}}/order-notes/interpretation
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "notes": "Vegan, extra spicy curry, contactless delivery please"
}
